<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="idols-for-restoration-druid-healer-phase-3">Idols for Restoration Druid Healer Phase 3</h4>Phase 3 introduces <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47671/idol-of-flaring-growth">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_relics_idolofrejuvenation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Flaring Growth</span></a>, a powerful throughput option for the idol slot. It's internal cooldown is significantly shorter than its buff duration, so constant uptime can be expected while you have rejuvenations active.<br/>
<br/>While it looks amazing, replacing <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40342/idol-of-awakening">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thegoldencheep.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Awakening</span></a> should be one of the last swaps you make to increase throughput. The regen returns are just that strong. <br/>
<br/>ToGC is a trash-less raid with plenty of downtime between bosses, so your regen needs could quickly become a non-issue, allowing you to swap in <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47671/idol-of-flaring-growth">
